- op: discuss  # f0e6
  at: '2026-11-18T02:17:17Z'  # f0e6
  by: agent  # f0e6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f0e6
  clock: 4  # f0e6
  nonce: f0e6  # f0e6
  message: "Done in PR #2245 (dev f7db4fce2). scripts/scheduled-gate holds the rule; scripts/auto-pr asks it before pushing and before each of its two merges; a block records blocked_scheduled_red and exits 1. THE DECISIONS THE ITEM ASKED TO BE WRITTEN DOWN (they are in the script's docstring): a change passes a red run by a commit trailer 'Fixes-scheduled-run: <red step>' (in history, where a wrong claim can be read later; a dependency-caused red is fixed by a PR that names the step all the same); the block lifts when commits on the base since the red verdict's commit carry that trailer for EVERY red step, and returns with the next red verdict, judged against that verdict's own commit; only the full suite blocks, a red nightly leg is reported and blocks nothing; a change to tracker data alone is exempt (tracker auto-sync does not go through auto-pr in any case); release PRs are merged by a person and are not gated; merge-pr does NOT ask the gate (governance file outside the owner's pre-approval; AGENTS.md now says not to use it to merge past a red run; gating it is the owner's call). EVIDENCE. Tests against real git repositories (tests/test_scheduled_gate.py, 24: green, five kinds of not-known, red blocked, the trailer naming a red step / another step / no trailer, tracker-only and mixed and empty changes, the lift for one of two and for both red steps, the block returning at the next red verdict, a verdict for a commit the clone lacks, fetch failure, as a process exit 3) and of auto-pr's wiring (tests/test_auto_pr.py TestScheduledRunGate, 5). 19 mutations, each red. LIVE: (a) the PR that merged this ran the new auto-pr: its log has 'scheduled gate: the full suite passed at fc2d2d8a (under an hour ago)' twice, before the push and before the merge. (b) the script against this repository with a RED verdict planted in a LOCAL ref only (refs/remotes/gatecheck/badges, deleted afterwards; nothing pushed): exit 3 and 'MERGING IS STOPPED while the last scheduled full run is red ... Fixes-scheduled-run: test-all-packages' (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/gate/live_red.txt). THE LIVE HALF THE CLOSE CONDITION NAMES IS NOT SHOWN: no scheduled run has been red since the verdicts began to publish, so no real auto-pr run has been refused, and none naming a step has merged through a red run. The first red verdict is that test."  # f0e6
